Why Are POI Substrates Becoming Important in Semiconductor Manufacturing?

Piezo-on-insulator substrates combine piezoelectric materials with insulating layers and supporting substrate structures to enable specialized electronic device fabrication. These material configurations can support device characteristics involving acoustic performance, electrical isolation and integration capabilities.

POI technologies are particularly relevant to RF components and acoustic-wave devices, where substrate characteristics influence device performance and fabrication requirements. Their use across specialized semiconductor applications is contributing to growing interest in advanced piezoelectric materials.

Market Growth Is Closely Linked to 5G and Advanced RF Filter Demand

The expansion of 5G infrastructure and wireless communication technologies is an important factor influencing POI substrate market development. Modern communication systems require RF components capable of supporting increasingly demanding frequency, bandwidth and signal-processing requirements.

POI materials are relevant to advanced filter technologies and specialized RF component manufacturing. SemiconductorInsight identifies commercialization of 5G, higher operating frequencies, wider bandwidth requirements and expanding RF applications among factors supporting market growth.

