Lithium niobate on insulator (LNOI) and lithium tantalate on insulator (LTOI) represent important material technologies within the POI market. These materials provide piezoelectric characteristics that can support specialized semiconductor and RF device applications.

The development of thin-film piezoelectric materials and substrate integration technologies is influencing the evolution of POI manufacturing. Different material configurations provide capabilities depending on device requirements, fabrication processes and integration approaches.

